/given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Amino acid catabolism by perfused rat hindquarter. The metabolic fates of valine.</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><volume>233</volume><fpage>621</fpage><lpage>630</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3085650</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000595-Lutz1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lutz</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name><name><surname>Viola</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Malikova</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Confort-Gouny</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ranjeva</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>A branched-chain organic acid linked to multiple sclerosis: First identification by NMR spectroscopy of CSF.</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><volume>354</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>164</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17217913</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000595-Hoffmann1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Jakobs</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmes</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Becker</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Organic acids in cerebrospinal fluid and plasma of patients with L-2-hydroxyglutaric aciduria.</article-title><source>J Inherit Metab Dis</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>193</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7564243</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000595-Letto1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"